  "schema": 3,
  "target_level": 2,
  "area": "system edges",
  "about": "Expected result-block values for the Ledgerine rehearsal ROM and the release ROM's auto QA run, judged by tools/judge.py. Block layout: arm9/source/game/ledger.h. Every item reads a flag word (values[1..7]) filled by one room's audit and carries \"done\": the completion bit of that room in values[0] (the rooms-complete items read values[0] itself, qa-verdict reads values[48]; the press-min boot has its own block, id LDPM). \"frame\" is the minimum number of frames to run, per boot. \"known\" lists, per emulator version and renderer, the gating items expected to fail there; judge.py --profile passes only when the failing set matches exactly. The BIOS items (rule book) grade the BIOS the emulator runs: headless melonDS and the profiles here use its built-in replacement BIOS, a real BIOS dump can differ.",
  "block": {
    "address": "0x0237F000",
    "magic": 1380275779
  },
  "boots": {
    "rehearsal": {
      "rom": "ledgerine-rehearsal.nds",
      "item_id": 1213350988,
      "item_id_text": "LDRH",
      "frames": 300,
      "note": "every room's audit in order; no save chip, no NitroFS"
    },
    "qa": {
      "rom": "ledgerine.nds",
      "item_id": 1314013521,
      "item_id_text": "QARN",
      "frames": 4000,
      "note": "the release ROM's hidden auto QA mode (title: hold L+R+X+Y for 120 frames): all six rooms played by key script, the credits; the block uses the rehearsal's layout and adds the QA words at values[48..54] (verdict 1 PASS / 2 FAIL, log lines, SD flags, last state hash, checkpoints, lag, save flags)"
    },
    "press-min": {
      "rom": "ledgerine-press-min.nds",
      "item_id": 1297105996,
      "item_id_text": "LDPM",
      "frames": 120,
      "note": "the 64-bit divider overflow check alone (-2^63 / -1, mode 2): DeSmuME's divider hangs the emulator on it, so the rehearsal and the QA run never run it; a CI that grades DeSmuME skips this ROM"
    }
  },
  "sources": {
    "GBATEK": "documented hardware behaviour; gating",
    "report:<ref>": "a hardware report by a third party (e.g. report:melonDS#2008); gating",
    "hw:<model>": "measured by us on real hardware; gating",
    "rom": "decided by the ROM's own deterministic logic, independent of the emulator; gating",
    "unconfirmed": "no hardware value yet; informational only, never fails the run"
  },
